---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../components/marketing/LegalShell.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout title="Terms and Conditions" description="ATW.Net terms of service for ATW One, ATW Orbit, Hub, Mail, Auth, Pay, Directory, and related products." canonical="https://atw.net/terms">
  <LegalShell title="Terms and Conditions" effective="November 5, 2026">
    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. Agreement and acceptance</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        These Terms and Conditions (the "Terms") are a binding agreement between you and No Name Marketing, LLC, doing business as ATW.Net ("ATW," "we," "us," or "our"), operating from 13940 Cedar Rd 438, University Heights, OH 44118-3204, USA.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        By creating an ATW account, joining an organization workspace, clicking to accept these Terms, or accessing or using ATW.Net products and services, you agree to these Terms on behalf of yourself and, if applicable, the organization you represent. If you do not agree, do not use the services.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        If you use the services on behalf of a company or other entity, you represent that you have authority to bind that entity to these Terms. In that case, "you" and "Customer" refer to that entity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. Accounts and organizations</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        You must provide accurate registration information and keep it current. You are responsible for safeguarding credentials, API keys, and other access materials associated with your account and organization, and for all activity that occurs under them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Organization administrators control membership, roles, and billing settings for their workspace. You must ensure that users you invite have a legitimate business need for access and that you have authority to bind the organization for fees and these Terms.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Notify us promptly at <a href="mailto:support@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">support@atw.net</a> if you suspect unauthorized access. We may require additional verification to protect accounts and organizations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. Services description</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        ATW provides cloud software and related services under the ATW.Net brand. Products may include, without limitation:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <li>ATW One: a Credits-based ERP and CRM workspace for customers, sales, finance, operations, and related business workflows</li>
        <li>ATW Orbit: productivity apps such as mail, calendar, office, and meetings (where offered). ATW Orbit capabilities (calendar, documents, meetings, messaging), where offered, are part of every paid ATW plan and draw from the organization Credits pool rather than a separate per-user seat price.</li>
        <li>Hub, Mail, Auth, Pay, and Directory: platform and supporting services for identity, messaging, payments, and directory features</li>
        <li>One AI / Agents: AI-assisted features and agent tooling that draw on organization Credits and configuration where enabled</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Features, availability, and product names may change over time. We may offer trials, beta or preview features, and optional add-ons. Beta and preview features are provided as-is and may be modified or withdrawn without notice. Marketing pages describe current offerings at a high level; the services you actually receive are those enabled for your organization under your plan and settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        You may use the services only for lawful business purposes and in accordance with these Terms, our policies, and applicable law. You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Attempt unauthorized access to accounts, systems, or data, or probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of our systems without written permission</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the services, other customers, or underlying infrastructure</li>
        <li>Upload malware, or use the services to distribute spam, phishing, or other abusive communications</li>
        <li>Misrepresent identity or affiliation, or use the services to violate others' intellectual property, privacy, or other rights</li>
        <li>Resell, sublicense, or provide the services to third parties except as expressly allowed in a written agreement with ATW</li>
        <li>Use AI or automation features in ways that violate law, these Terms, or the rights of others, or to generate content you present as human-authored where disclosure is legally required</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        We may investigate suspected violations and suspend or terminate access where we reasonably believe abuse, legal risk, or harm to the platform or other customers has occurred or is likely.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Customer data and confidentiality</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        As between you and ATW, you (and your organization) own the data, content, and materials you or your users submit to the services ("Customer Data"). These Terms do not transfer ownership of Customer Data to ATW.
